  "text": "The Amazon's net contribution to the oxygen you breathe is roughly zero. It does make enormous amounts of oxygen. That part is completely true. But a forest is not only leaves. It is everything eating and rotting inside it. Every animal, every root, every fungus is breathing that oxygen straight back in. So the books balance almost exactly. Made and used in the same place. Most of the oxygen you actually breathe came out of the sea anyway. None of which makes the Amazon less important. It makes it important differently. It is a colossal carbon store. It also makes most of its own rainfall. Losing it would be a catastrophe. Just not the one everybody names. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
